{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/815288-invictus","id":815288,"title":"Invictus","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-23T23:54:08-08:00","id":815288,"title":"Invictus","content":"How does one get the ability to hand out territory? All the merits are about being under someone, how do you be the someone? <br /> <br /> I don't have my book to copy paste specifically..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T01:01:24-08:00","id":815303,"title":"","content":"If you're getting territory handed out to you, you most likely have City or sometimes Covenant status high enough to have been granted that land. The land itself is probably best represented by a combination of the Feeding Grounds and Equipment, though I have no advice on how to model it with the latter.<br /> <br /> As for how you get there, it's probably going to be a matter of plot. You work for the city or covenant, you rise up in the ranks, and with those greater responsibilities you get greater perks, including the possibility of the rights and privilege to run part of the domain.<br /> <br /> I feel like I'm missing part of your question, so if you want to clarify something I didn't talk about, feel free!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T04:03:02-08:00","id":815347,"title":"","content":"I think Vitalis is talking about the Oaths of Serfdom in Invictus. Well, it's simple, your underlings take the merit, and you get the benefits of that merit's land owners status without paying anything yourself <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T07:53:33-08:00","id":815447,"title":"","content":"Griautis is right. The boss never has to pay for Oaths. Just find some sucker willing to swear an Oath to you, have them pay their Merit dots, then you get the boss half of the benefits. The only cost on your end is finding the underling and convincing them.<br /> <br /> In fact, the Invictus merit section says that having someone sworn to you in this fashion is a prerequisite to being considered a full member of the Covenant.<br /> <br /> Might be a good thing to use your coterie for, since they benefit both parties generally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T08:18:40-08:00","id":815468,"title":"","content":"In a traditional Invictus neo-feudal setup, the Prince would own all of the territory within her city, simply because she's the sovereign. Then the Clan Prisci all swear Oaths of Serfdom to her, subdividing the city into large swaths of territory for each Clan. Then anyone who wants personal territory of their own swears an Oath of Serfdom to his Clan's Priscus, further parceling out the land.<br /> <br /> Of course, in practice it's rarely that rigidly structured, especially in Domains that aren't ruled by the Invictus. Often the highest ranking Invictus in a city will simply secure a large chunk of territory for the Covenant, by what ever means the local Court uses to distribute territory. Then they'll subdivide that territory among their members in a similar pyramid scheme.<br /> <br /> EDIT: It occurred to me you might be asking more about Invictus Oaths than territory distribution. The only requirement to be the liege in an Oath is a dot of Invictus status, and someone willing to buy the Merit and swear the Oath to you. A good reputation and High Status within the Invictus and within the city might help potential vassals feel more comfortable swearing an Oath to you, but it's not a requirement. For the Oath of Serfdom specifically, you have to own the territory you intend to parcel out. How one acquires territory varies by domain, but within Invictus domains it's usually by swearing an Oath of Serfdom to a higher-ranking memer of the court, and if you follow the chain back far enough, it leads to the Prince.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-24-2016, 11:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T20:39:01-08:00","id":815860,"title":"","content":"Very helpful. Thank you. I had a terribly vague question and elderand was able to really able to answer. I was more asking if as a player I wanted to hand out land what kind of merits I needed.. Since there is only the merit to take stuff, how can you be the giver. I guess. You just need to be Invictus... <br /> <br /> Sorry I was vague!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}